{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1420194-population-growth-in-mystic-paradigm-parallel-world","id":1420194,"title":"Population growth in mystic paradigm parallel world","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-10-25T18:53:56-07:00","id":1420194,"title":"Population growth in mystic paradigm parallel world","content":"Suppose you wanted to increase population in a world without factories and technologically driven agriculture. Human labor with simple tools or animal driven plows are part of this world's Consensus. You want to produce Enough Food for a growing population. A certain portion of this could come from Magick effects, but you want to allow sleepers to be reasonably self-sufficient. The creatures that WoD Void Engineers destroyed or banished still live on this world. The seven Mystical Traditions rule together and the Progenitors were never part of the Wick.<br /> <br /> How to?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-25T19:18:43-07:00","id":1420195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1420194-population-growth-in-mystic-paradigm-parallel-world#post1420194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Suppose you wanted to increase population in a world without factories and technologically driven agriculture. Human labor with simple tools or animal driven plows are part of this world's Consensus. You want to produce Enough Food for a growing population. A certain portion of this could come from Magick effects, but you want to allow sleepers to be reasonably self-sufficient. The creatures that WoD Void Engineers destroyed or banished still live on this world. The seven Mystical Traditions rule together and the Progenitors were never part of the Wick.<br /> <br /> How to?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The same way the Order of Reason did it. By expanding the consensus. Magick is like Hyper science so there's Low and linear options for SLeepers. Honestly I don't see how the Order of Hermes doesn't become something like the order of reason Craftng their perfect cities ruled by Mages... with even the most illiterate peasant knowing charms.. with magically enhanced animals plowing the fields.. with magically enhanced crops.. with proper balance of the elements to make the ground more productive..<br /> <br /> The Wu Lung would be even more so... industralization was readilly used in early china, they had no problem burning through people like that..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-26T16:20:10-07:00","id":1420342,"title":"","content":"I\u2019ll think they\u2019ll be much less population growth without industrial revolution.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-26T16:40:39-07:00","id":1420348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1420194-population-growth-in-mystic-paradigm-parallel-world?p=1420342#post1420342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019ll think they\u2019ll be much less population growth without industrial revolution.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> But the Order of Hermes or Wu lung COULD push an Industrial Revolution.. it would just look... different. Not every Paradigm could provide a robust set of options ot sleepers but many could and did. China was historically much closer to what we think of as &quot;Industrialized&quot; until relatively recently, thus why it the East tended to have MUCH larger cities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-26T18:25:12-07:00","id":1420369,"title":"","content":"Remind me again. Isn't the order of hermes based on mystery cults, cloistered in their towers?<br /> <br /> Seems like they aren't the kind of guys who would push 'disseminate magic to the common man'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-26T18:34:11-07:00","id":1420372,"title":"","content":"That's why the Order of Reason formed: former members of the Order of Hermes got fed up with that attitude and struck out on their own. <br /> <br /> Now imagine an alternate universe where the Craftmasons managed to persuade the Order of Hermes to back their initiative to put magic into the hands of the common man.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-26T18:54:52-07:00","id":1420381,"title":"","content":"To be frank? Mostly the same as before. Maybe there's the different tech trees and methods of projection, and maybe more centralization.<br /> <br /> But either way, there's the ascension war as always.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-26T19:53:40-07:00","id":1420391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1420194-population-growth-in-mystic-paradigm-parallel-world?p=1420342#post1420342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019ll think they\u2019ll be much less population growth without industrial revolution.</div> </div> </div> </div>See, this is what I'm thinking. My picture of the prehistoric era is one where the proportion of Mages to Sleepers was way different than in a world whose population is approaching eight billion. In contemporary WoD, there are no natural predators left that threaten humans, at least not any that wouldn't die of paradox in an attempt to hunt openly. Apathy rules, according to the books. Apathy is soul-eroding. Sleepers in default WoD, it could be suggested, have weaker Avatars. It sounds rather judgemental, but so is saying that apathy rules.<br /> <br /> In a world where a prehistoric man uses the blessing of a Verbena sorceress to cross the territory of an Umbrood predator to return to his young love, Sleepers' avatars would be stronger. If you advance that to the era before Order of Reason got going, the parallel world would still have Sleepers with stronger avatars, more mages per-capita. <br /> <br /> Since it is rather hard to bring armies of sleepers through a Sidestep Time or Spirit effect, there might actually be a balance that would prevent the Technocracy from invading the parallel world. Add to that the fact that not all mystic creatures were predators on humans. The Traditions would certainly have some dragons (a la game of Thrones) and giants who are their allies. I realize I did not discuss conflict between the parallel worlds' ruling Mage factions in the initial question. It is something I am considering in relation to population and capacity to raise defenses. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1420194-population-growth-in-mystic-paradigm-parallel-world?p=1420348#post1420348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> But the Order of Hermes or Wu lung COULD push an Industrial Revolution.. it would just look... different. Not every Paradigm could provide a robust set of options ot sleepers but many could and did. China was historically much closer to what we think of as &quot;Industrialized&quot; until relatively recently, thus why it the East tended to have MUCH larger cities.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does pushing an industrial paradigm produce the same result as the Technocracy achieved? The Hermetics' idea is that you meaningfully speak words, make gestures and reality adapts to you will. Would industrial production conflict with that? Why would you have people packed together, doing repetitive tasks if you could meet human needs through linguistic command of reality? Or, why cast Magick words if you have a factory? I'm waiting for Technocracy Reloaded to see what it says about the Technocracy in China. Have no idea how to order a physical copy through a book store.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1420194-population-growth-in-mystic-paradigm-parallel-world?p=1420369#post1420369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Remind me again. Isn't the order of hermes based on mystery cults, cloistered in their towers?<br /> <br /> Seems like they aren't the kind of guys who would push 'disseminate magic to the common man'.</div> </div> </div> </div>They are described in all kinds of ways, because they go all the way back to Ars Magica. If each person is supposed to discover a special word that represents them, it might be hard to teach every single person how to use Magick according to their unique individual perspective. It's also about passing difficult tests. They were competitive. <br /> <br /> Mage has an offense-default. If you meet another Mage and you can't easily identify them as being part of your faction, at the very least, you will want to cast an effect that stops them from shredding your pattern first. The Hermetics had the Parma-Magica, a spell that temporarily cuts you off from casting, but makes you immune to that of another Mage. That's why they became so dominant, compared to other Traditions. <br /> <br /> The invention of the printing press makes mystery cults difficult to sustain. The UK government used to have Freemasons throughout it. This interfered with the normal operation of government, because knowing the rhyme-scheme gave you a guarantee of passing the selection interview when someone more competent did not. Newspapers blew that wide open. The British public wanted a functioning government that served citizens equally, and so Masons were purged from the ranks of the civil service. Now, books about formerly secret rites of introduction can be borrowed from almost any public library. <br /> <br /> Appeal by exclusivity still draws people into that sort of thing. It is just that, using Masons as an example, why would most men want to be part of a group that places demands on your time, where there is no chance of meeting women? Whatever downside a group would have previously been able to hide from potential recruits, the printing press ensures will come to light. If you can get the last mystery from the library, there is no reason to regularly sneak off to the lodge and debase yourself. We assume that Masons in WoD would have an overlap of Hermetics, NWO and others competing to run the organization. <br /> <br /> The Verbena use a degree of appeal by exclusivity. At least there may be dating prospects - sex magick, for example. Returning to the subject of population growth, maybe sex-Magick would be essential to that goal. Druidic rituals to bless warriors before confronting the rampaging giant. Hit it with lightning to soften it up. Sacrifice the giant to promote fertility. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-26T20:22:21-07:00","id":1420392,"title":"","content":"Question.<br /> <br /> ..... Ok, its been a long time since I read the books. Is there any philosophical or mental or just plain ass exclusivity needed?<br /> <br /> In the eyes of an akashic, verbena, or hermetic. Do you have to be 'special' in any way to use Magick?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-26T23:14:01-07:00","id":1420407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1420194-population-growth-in-mystic-paradigm-parallel-world?p=1420392#post1420392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question.<br /> <br /> ..... Ok, its been a long time since I read the books. Is there any philosophical or mental or just plain ass exclusivity needed?<br /> <br /> In the eyes of an akashic, verbena, or hermetic. Do you have to be 'special' in any way to use Magick?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's all about the Avatar. The avatar is a special gift. Mentors teach Focus to Mages who have already been visited by their Avatar. There are some other ways things can happen. <br /> <br /> 1. The avatar hasn't appeared yet, but is destined to arrive and the precogniscient mentor eagerly recruits the soon-to-be Mage. <br /> <br /> 2. With great effort or good luck, a mentor turns a sleeper who would not have awakened into a Mage. The teaching creates the circumstance under which the otherwise-absent avatar shows up.<br /> <br /> 3. Let's say FACADE just shipped a vat-grown human over to The NWO's Mind-crafting facility. They craft a personality and reference-memory for the new person. They are not awakened or gifted with visitation from their avatar. The Operatives need awakened Mages right now. In this case, the mentor does something drastic to force awakening to occur. The avatar shows up in response. <br /> <br /> Besides having an Avatar, there are all kinds of ways a person could be Special that don't guarantee a chance at Awakening. The easiest criteria to use is Intelligence. If the person has lived in a Consensus that excludes a particular kind of Magick, high intelligence could make them harder to be trained into awakening by a well intentioned mentor. They have internalized the Consensus Paradigm and their high intelligence makes them a better skeptic, preventing the mentor from imparting wisdom. When filling out a Mage character sheet, as long as you have determined this character is going to be a Mage, there is no minimum number of dots you need to add to any stat, beyond what the rules prescribe.<br /> <br /> For the convenience of running a game, all the players are recruited by mentors of the same faction (Technocracy/Traditions). The awakening happens and it is within one faction's territory or they receive a call to go to a special place. The players work together. <br /> <br /> As a storyteller, I see it on a timeline where the character's Avatar visits them for the first time, initiating a Seeking, a sort of mission. The experience opens them to understanding that they can change things with their will. The Questing Avatar might only need to appear once, but has the highest single demand, &quot;Save the world&quot;, &quot;Build a space colony on Mars&quot;. It's not the end goal, but striving to achieve this that makes the Mage advance in his Arete and Spheres. Pattern, I think, shows up when you are done the last Seeking to give you a new one built on the achievements of the last - well ordered, achievable goals. Dynamic - change the world around you, make a difference in the life of someone stuck in a rut. Primordial, you are an incarnation of a concept, so go represent that in the world. <br /> <br /> The character may have done some Magick-type things before being aware of their avatar. They survived a car accident that should have killed them, having unconsciously or reflexively used an effect. <br /> <br /> There are ways that you can make a Special thing about the person a driver of the Awakening. <br /> Akashic: Early adversity breeds future success.<br /> Verbena - Gardeners of The Tree: They have a hereditary gift for Magick. <br /> Hermetic: A gift for language or math.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-26T23:33:29-07:00","id":1420410,"title":"","content":"I mean philosophically. Their paradigm. Their consensus.<br /> <br /> Because remember. One of the most key factors in the technocracy is 'anyone can do what we do, so long as they have the knowledge, machinery, and expertise we have.'<br /> <br /> As magic systems go, it's relatively egalitarian and neutral.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-27T00:28:08-07:00","id":1420414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1420194-population-growth-in-mystic-paradigm-parallel-world?p=1420410#post1420410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean philosophically. Their paradigm. Their consensus.<br /> <br /> Because remember. One of the most key factors in the technocracy is 'anyone can do what we do, so long as they have the knowledge, machinery, and expertise we have.'<br /> <br /> As magic systems go, it's relatively egalitarian and neutral.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you want to interpret a Technocrat's optimistic invitation literally, as a storyteller, have huge numbers of Sleepers awakening in training facilities. I would find that chronicle hard to run. I set a hard limit of 1 per 10,000 where a high concentration of Mages is necessary for the plot, as low as 1 per 100,000 where the plot isn't centered.<br /> <br /> Near the end of every Convention book, there are notable characters. Their backstory usually defines them with some kind of special quality or life experience. The point is, if the person wasn't chosen by their avatar or the avatar is unwilling, the training will only make them whatever the Technocracy term for Acolyte is. They can't do Magick, but seeing it doesn't cause the caster Paradox.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-27T05:43:30-07:00","id":1420436,"title":"","content":"Extraordinary Citizens. They're capable of using Wonders (and, in MRev, were also capable of learning Linear \u201ctechno-sorcery\u201d), but lack the fully versatility of Enlightened Science. <br /> <br /> Arguably, the trick that the Order of Reason hit upon was the ability to efficiently distill Enlightened Procedures into Wonders or Paths that could be used by their Extraordinary Citizens (or whatever they called them back then), and then to distill them even further to the point that they were fully integrated into the Consensus and could be used by anyone simply through the application of appropriate Abilities and gear, with no need for Spheres <i>or</i> Paths. <br /> <br /> Whether or not that's restricted to the trappings of technology depends on whether the Storyteller thinks that the Technocracy might be right and that Enlightened Science takes the forms it does because it's building on the foundational truth of reality. If not, then there's no reason in principle why the aforementioned distillation from Sphere to Path to \u201clow magic\u201d couldn't be applied to the Hermetic Focus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-27T15:08:44-07:00","id":1420554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1420194-population-growth-in-mystic-paradigm-parallel-world?p=1420436#post1420436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Extraordinary Citizens.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's it. I use the abbreviation EC all the time when writing character reference descriptions. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1420194-population-growth-in-mystic-paradigm-parallel-world?p=1420436#post1420436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whether or not that's restricted to the trappings of technology depends on whether the Storyteller thinks that the Technocracy might be right and that Enlightened Science takes the forms it does because it's building on the foundational truth of reality. If not, then there's no reason in principle why the aforementioned distillation from Sphere to Path to \u201clow magic\u201d couldn't be applied to the Hermetic Focus.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is one thing that I find interesting to ponder about this. From what I remember, the permanent investment into Wonders is Willpower. The caster sacrifices some of his will to make the McGuffin. If it is Hermetics, who are incredibly competitive, depleting your willpower could diminish your ability to advance. So, the Mage creating Wonders would have the expectation that he is protected during the time he is recovering, in game terms, spending xp to raise his willpower.<br /> <br /> It gets even more interesting when you consider NWO making techno-gadgets for their ECs. The master-machinist is surrounded by people whose Affinity Sphere is Mind. <br /> <br /> &quot;Hey, can you make this gadget for my team? I'll pay you a million dollars and some quint.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Okay.&quot;<br /> <br /> Some time later, &quot;Hey, I was really desperate when I asked you for that gadget. Why don't you give me back $750,000. I need it to do the important work on the ground.&quot; - Mind 3.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-27T15:41:10-07:00","id":1420568,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the technocracy really looks down on people doing that and often the audits come out the end of a gun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-27T16:01:23-07:00","id":1420571,"title":"","content":"The technocracy got around the willpower problem by discovering a way to make gadgets without expending willpower to do so. I'm a bit more leery of the idea of the Order of Hermes duplicating that feat: I tend to think that it was The Syndicate and their money magic that discovered the secret, though it may have been iteration X and their notion of mass production.<br /> <br /> If the loophole is based on Mass production, there may be no way to deal with it. The predecessors to iteration X May well be the only group that would have thought of such a thing.<br /> <br /> But if the loophole is based on the Syndicate's money magic, it turns out that the Celestial Chorus has a surprisingly similar view. I could see their predecessors developing something not unlike Primal Utility, but focused through faith rather than economics. With that, an alliance between the Order of Hermes and the Celestial Chorus could produce the massive amount of Wonders needed. Certainly, the Syndicate's ability to harvest Primal Energy from Primal Ventures was a major contributing factor to the Technocracy's massive surplus of Quintessence needed to construct so many Wonders.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-28T15:59:02-07:00","id":1420721,"title":"","content":"I think that it's as simple as making Effects so accepted in the Consensus - so hard-coded into what people think is possible - that is ceases to be &quot;Magic&quot; in any form, and starts just being &quot;Thing You Do&quot;.<br /> <br /> You know, like driving a car. Cars used to be Rotes/Wonders by technomancers, and/or dedicated Instruments for casting Path of Conveyance spells. Now it's entirely a function of the Drive ability. No Willpower expenditure, Awakening, or instruction in linear Sorcery required. (Even the creation of a car is more a function of the Technology ability, albeit one so complicated no single person can do it all themselves).<br /> <br /> There's an argument that can be made (because I've done so in the past) that large swaths of what people consider &quot;normal human feats&quot; were once True Magick, that just became so normalized that Reality doesn't recognize them as &quot;magic&quot; anymore. Building a fire from rubbing sticks together is Forces/Hellfire, until everyone was doing it. Talking is functionally a method of telepathy, using grunts and inflections to put ideas into other people's heads.<br /> <br /> All the Order of Reason did was introduce new technologies and techniques, popularizing and supporting them long enough for the &quot;kinks&quot; to be worked out (read: make it stop invoking Paradox or require Willpower to use). Academic, media, and economic factors helped, as did mass production, but they were means to an end. That end being turning it Coincidental.<br /> <br /> If the Order of Hermes were inclined to do the same thing, we would see mass adoption of things like golems or invisible conjured workers tilling the fields or doing manual labor, instead of tractors or forklifts. If people really believe in the spells to build or conjure workers (either spirits or programmed masses of invisible force), they could be taught to do it themselves in more concentrated ways. (I recommend looking into the OSR book <a href=\"https://youtu.be/-k07cDMepfU\" target=\"_blank\">Magical Industrial Revolution</a>, which illustrates how wizardry could be brought to industrial proportions.)<br /> <br /> Same with things like magic brooms or flying carpets to convey people around, or magic mirrors to facilitate long-distance communication.<br /> <br /> One could argue that a Hermetic industrial society would require skilled magician-artisans to keep going. I would argue that we already have that kind of thing in the real world. Our society would grind to a halt without the legions of engineers, mechanics, technicians, programmers, and experts that maintain our machines and systems. In a Hermetic industrial society, it would be the same, except with more wand waving and arcane sigils.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":6156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","user":"Bluecho","date":". 10-28-2020, 07:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-28T20:58:21-07:00","id":1420761,"title":"","content":"We've got some guidelines as to what it takes to make something Coincidental; and I could definitely see uses of Magick to make Procedures available to Extraordinary Citizens (see my thread about <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1263470-spellbooks\">Spellbooks</a> for some thoughts on how the Wonder Crafting rules could be adapted to allow Extraordinary Citizens to learn and use Procedures). But I wonder what it would take to bring it to that final step of being \u201csomething that anyone with the right Ability and tools can do\u201d? I mean, that goes beyond making it Coincidental, and beyond creating \u201cSleeper Magic\u201d (Sorcery/Hedge Magic, if you wish; or <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/3491-acolyte-magic\">Acolyte Magic</a>, if you don't want to use a whole separate system to handle Sleepers with magic). Once you've got those factors in place, what does it take to remove the need to spend experience points on arcane powers and fully integrated them into the natural order of things? <br /> <br /> This is a concept I've tackled in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1363729-work-in-progress\">Work in Progress</a>; but sadly, that thread is still more aptly named than I'd like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-29T14:04:19-07:00","id":1420865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1420194-population-growth-in-mystic-paradigm-parallel-world?p=1420721#post1420721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that it's as simple as making Effects so accepted in the Consensus - so hard-coded into what people think is possible - that is ceases to be &quot;Magic&quot; in any form, and starts just being &quot;Thing You Do&quot;.<br /> <br /> You know, like driving a car. Cars used to be Rotes/Wonders by technomancers, and/or dedicated Instruments for casting Path of Conveyance spells. Now it's entirely a function of the Drive ability. No Willpower expenditure, Awakening, or instruction in linear Sorcery required. (Even the creation of a car is more a function of the Technology ability, albeit one so complicated no single person can do it all themselves).<br /> <br /> There's an argument that can be made (because I've done so in the past) that large swaths of what people consider &quot;normal human feats&quot; were once True Magick, that just became so normalized that Reality doesn't recognize them as &quot;magic&quot; anymore. Building a fire from rubbing sticks together is Forces/Hellfire, until everyone was doing it. Talking is functionally a method of telepathy, using grunts and inflections to put ideas into other people's heads.<br /> <br /> All the Order of Reason did was introduce new technologies and techniques, popularizing and supporting them long enough for the &quot;kinks&quot; to be worked out (read: make it stop invoking Paradox or require Willpower to use). Academic, media, and economic factors helped, as did mass production, but they were means to an end. That end being turning it Coincidental.<br /> <br /> If the Order of Hermes were inclined to do the same thing, we would see mass adoption of things like golems or invisible conjured workers tilling the fields or doing manual labor, instead of tractors or forklifts. If people really believe in the spells to build or conjure workers (either spirits or programmed masses of invisible force), they could be taught to do it themselves in more concentrated ways. (I recommend looking into the OSR book <a href=\"https://youtu.be/-k07cDMepfU\" target=\"_blank\">Magical Industrial Revolution</a>, which illustrates how wizardry could be brought to industrial proportions.)<br /> <br /> Same with things like magic brooms or flying carpets to convey people around, or magic mirrors to facilitate long-distance communication.<br /> <br /> One could argue that a Hermetic industrial society would require skilled magician-artisans to keep going. I would argue that we already have that kind of thing in the real world. Our society would grind to a halt without the legions of engineers, mechanics, technicians, programmers, and experts that maintain our machines and systems. In a Hermetic industrial society, it would be the same, except with more wand waving and arcane sigils.</div> </div> </div> </div>There might be an argument against this &quot;putting Magick in the hand of common men&quot;. Namely, it is counter-productive to developing the heights of True Magick. Wouldn't Awakenings plummet down once magic was made easily learnable?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-29T14:16:31-07:00","id":1420868,"title":"","content":"Have they, though? Remember, Bluecho's premise is that the Technocracy did exactly this: they put Magick in the hands of common men. Has that made Awakenings more rare?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-29T15:47:49-07:00","id":1420879,"title":"","content":"Exactly. That's why I said &quot;If the Order of Hermes were inclined to do the same thing...&quot;. If the Order of Hermes were to have a change of priorities to that of the Order of Reason, they could have leveraged their Paradigm into one that brought the world into an industrial standard of living.<br /> <br /> Just, you know, different in form (though not function) to the one we &quot;enjoy&quot; today.<br /> <br /> For another examination of what a Hermetic industrial world order would look like, see the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bartimaeus_Sequence\" target=\"_blank\">Bartimaeus Series</a> by Jonathan Stroud.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-30T10:34:24-07:00","id":1421003,"title":"","content":"Do we really <i>know </i>that Awakenings are rarer than they were before? Mages don't seem to have exactly been common even pre-OoR and they were a minority even in Horizon.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1420194-population-growth-in-mystic-paradigm-parallel-world?p=1420554#post1420554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It gets even more interesting when you consider NWO making techno-gadgets for their ECs. The master-machinist is surrounded by people whose Affinity Sphere is Mind.<br /> <br /> &quot;Hey, can you make this gadget for my team? I'll pay you a million dollars and some quint.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Okay.&quot;<br /> <br /> Some time later, &quot;Hey, I was really desperate when I asked you for that gadget. Why don't you give me back $750,000. I need it to do the important work on the ground.&quot; - Mind 3.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Affinity sphere&quot; =/= &quot;automatically better than all other factions at this sphere&quot;.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1410-czernobog","name":"Czernobog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-30T10:48:36-07:00","id":1421007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Czernobog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1420194-population-growth-in-mystic-paradigm-parallel-world?p=1421003#post1421003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do we really <i>know </i>that Awakenings are rarer than they were before?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, we don't know for certain.<br /> <br /> Albeit, in % of the population, they should have been more than 1:1000000 because otherwise you don't have enough people back then to fill all the factions with enough members (that's already challenging in out overpopulated world).<br /> <br /> But even *IF* they were rarer now, we wouldn't know if the reason it's Paradigmatical, or maybe it's because the amount of new strong Avatars can't keep with the population increase, or because the Psychopomps were more active, or...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-30T22:50:21-07:00","id":1421119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Czernobog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1420194-population-growth-in-mystic-paradigm-parallel-world?p=1421003#post1421003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do we really <i>know </i>that Awakenings are rarer than they were before? Mages don't seem to have exactly been common even pre-OoR and they were a minority even in Horizon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Verbena Revised talks about the Wick and their Magickal descendants, the Aeduna, being Mages. It implies that there were many Mages compared to the small human population in prehistoric times. That's only counting the four groups that belonged to the Wick; Verbena, Dreamspeakers, Cult of Ecstasy and Cosian Circle (Progenitors). <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Czernobog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1420194-population-growth-in-mystic-paradigm-parallel-world?p=1421003#post1421003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Affinity sphere&quot; =/= &quot;automatically better than all other factions at this sphere&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't assume that, merely that they have at least one dot in it, with some methodologies having another affinity sphere. Many NWO have Mind at least to the level that they could use it on one of their own who has depleted willpower. So, the question of other factions doesn't come into play in the example. It would be a dirty thing to do to a loyal artificer, but construct-politics can be nasty. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-02T17:16:03-08:00","id":1421527,"title":"","content":"I hope this reply is not missing the topic.<br /> As far as I understand the starting of this topic, the question was how to increase the population in the described parallel world.<br /> The population would grow if somehow you could advance their health, e.g. because some deadly ilnneses don't exist (like multi resistant bacteria) or by growing healing herbs and increasing their healing power. People would get older, children would survive more often etc. Good nutrition would serve the same goal. Low levels of every day stress can help to keep the people healthy as well.<br /> And of course, if you can keep the people inside your faction from fighting with one another.<br /> Food and water supplies, health and safety I would assume as the most important factors for the growth of the population. Just those things at the bottom of the hierarchy of needs (as described by Maslow).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26246-caliginosa","name":"Caliginosa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-02T20:53:33-08:00","id":1421556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1420194-population-growth-in-mystic-paradigm-parallel-world?p=1420761#post1420761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(see my thread about <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1263470-spellbooks\">Spellbooks</a> for some thoughts on how the Wonder Crafting rules could be adapted to allow Extraordinary Citizens to learn and use Procedures).</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1420194-population-growth-in-mystic-paradigm-parallel-world?p=1420761#post1420761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Sorcery/Hedge Magic, if you wish; or <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/3491-acolyte-magic\">Acolyte Magic</a></div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b\u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1420194-population-growth-in-mystic-paradigm-parallel-world?p=1420761#post1420761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a concept I've tackled in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1363729-work-in-progress\">Work in Progress</a>; but sadly, that thread is still more aptly named than I'd like.</div> </div> </div> </div>I will check these in time.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1420194-population-growth-in-mystic-paradigm-parallel-world?p=1420721#post1420721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(I recommend looking into the OSR book <a href=\"https://youtu.be/-k07cDMepfU\" target=\"_blank\">Magical Industrial Revolution</a>, which illustrates how wizardry could be brought to industrial proportions.)</div> </div> </div> </div>This too<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1420194-population-growth-in-mystic-paradigm-parallel-world?p=1421007#post1421007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, we don't know for certain.<br /> <br /> Albeit, in % of the population, they should have been more than 1:1000000 because otherwise you don't have enough people back then to fill all the factions with enough members (that's already challenging in out overpopulated world).<br /> <br /> But even *IF* they were rarer now, we wouldn't know if the reason it's Paradigmatical, or maybe it's because the amount of new strong Avatars can't keep with the population increase, or because the Psychopomps were more active, or...</div> </div> </div> </div>Psychopomps, definitely something for me to brush up on.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caliginosa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1420194-population-growth-in-mystic-paradigm-parallel-world?p=1421527#post1421527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hope this reply is not missing the topic.<br /> As far as I understand the starting of this topic, the question was how to increase the population in the described parallel world.<br /> The population would grow if somehow you could advance their health, e.g. because some deadly ilnneses don't exist (like multi resistant bacteria) or by growing healing herbs and increasing their healing power. People would get older, children would survive more often etc. Good nutrition would serve the same goal. Low levels of every day stress can help to keep the people healthy as well.<br /> And of course, if you can keep the people inside your faction from fighting with one another.<br /> Food and water supplies, health and safety I would assume as the most important factors for the growth of the population. Just those things at the bottom of the hierarchy of needs (as described by Maslow).</div> </div> </div> </div>I will make a list from this. Thanks.<br /> <br /> Thank you to everyone who posted resources and ideas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-03T06:37:54-08:00","id":1421610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1420194-population-growth-in-mystic-paradigm-parallel-world?p=1420721#post1420721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that it's as simple as making Effects so accepted in the Consensus - so hard-coded into what people think is possible - that is ceases to be &amp;quot;Magic&amp;quot; in any form, and starts just being &amp;quot;Thing You Do&amp;quot;.<br /> <br /> You know, like driving a car. Cars used to be Rotes/Wonders by technomancers, and/or dedicated Instruments for casting Path of Conveyance spells. Now it's entirely a function of the Drive ability. No Willpower expenditure, Awakening, or instruction in linear Sorcery required. (Even the creation of a car is more a function of the Technology ability, albeit one so complicated no single person can do it all themselves).<br /> <br /> There's an argument that can be made (because I've done so in the past) that large swaths of what people consider &amp;quot;normal human feats&amp;quot; were once True Magick, that just became so normalized that Reality doesn't recognize them as &amp;quot;magic&amp;quot; anymore. Building a fire from rubbing sticks together is Forces/Hellfire, until everyone was doing it. Talking is functionally a method of telepathy, using grunts and inflections to put ideas into other people's heads.<br /> <br /> All the Order of Reason did was introduce new technologies and techniques, popularizing and supporting them long enough for the &amp;quot;kinks&amp;quot; to be worked out (read: make it stop invoking Paradox or require Willpower to use). Academic, media, and economic factors helped, as did mass production, but they were means to an end. That end being turning it Coincidental.<br /> <br /> If the Order of Hermes were inclined to do the same thing, we would see mass adoption of things like golems or invisible conjured workers tilling the fields or doing manual labor, instead of tractors or forklifts. If people really believe in the spells to build or conjure workers (either spirits or programmed masses of invisible force), they could be taught to do it themselves in more concentrated ways. (I recommend looking into the OSR book <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">https://youtu.be/-k07cDMepfU&amp;quot;]Magical</a> Industrial Revolution[/URL], which illustrates how wizardry could be brought to industrial proportions.)<br /> <br /> Same with things like magic brooms or flying carpets to convey people around, or magic mirrors to facilitate long-distance communication.<br /> <br /> One could argue that a Hermetic industrial society would require skilled magician-artisans to keep going. I would argue that we already have that kind of thing in the real world. Our society would grind to a halt without the legions of engineers, mechanics, technicians, programmers, and experts that maintain our machines and systems. In a Hermetic industrial society, it would be the same, except with more wand waving and arcane sigils.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1420194-population-growth-in-mystic-paradigm-parallel-world?p=1420761#post1420761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We've got some guidelines as to what it takes to make something Coincidental; and I could definitely see uses of Magick to make Procedures available to Extraordinary Citizens (see my thread about <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1263470-spellbooks\">Spellbooks</a> for some thoughts on how the Wonder Crafting rules could be adapted to allow Extraordinary Citizens to learn and use Procedures). But I wonder what it would take to bring it to that final step of being \u201csomething that anyone with the right Ability and tools can do\u201d? I mean, that goes beyond making it Coincidental, and beyond creating \u201cSleeper Magic\u201d (Sorcery/Hedge Magic, if you wish; or <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/3491-acolyte-magic\">Acolyte Magic</a>, if you don't want to use a whole separate system to handle Sleepers with magic). Once you've got those factors in place, what does it take to remove the need to spend experience points on arcane powers and fully integrated them into the natural order of things? <br /> <br /> This is a concept I've tackled in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1363729-work-in-progress\">Work in Progress</a>; but sadly, that thread is still more aptly named than I'd like.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd like to clarify something here: I'm disagreeing with Bluecho on a point. Namely, I don't think that \u201cmaking it Coincidental\u201d is enough. There are plenty of Effects out there that are Coincidental, but that Sleepers can't use. In other words \u201cmake it Coincidental\u201d is a necessary condition, but not a sufficient one. If you want to put magic in the hands of the common man, you need to do more than that. <br /> <br /> And that's where my comment above is coming from: it's an attempt to address the question of what more needs to be done.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-04T22:19:19-08:00","id":1421931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1420194-population-growth-in-mystic-paradigm-parallel-world?p=1421610#post1421610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> I'd like to clarify something here: I'm disagreeing with Bluecho on a point. Namely, I don't think that \u201cmaking it Coincidental\u201d is enough. There are plenty of Effects out there that are Coincidental, but that Sleepers can't use. In other words \u201cmake it Coincidental\u201d is a necessary condition, but not a sufficient one. If you want to put magic in the hands of the common man, you need to do more than that.<br /> <br /> And that's where my comment above is coming from: it's an attempt to address the question of what more needs to be done.</div> </div> </div> </div>Claim that you can do something that can be predicted to create moral opposition, but has some benefit. GMO agriculture is a perfect example, because it has already been put into the Consensus. In my head-canon, it is the Progenitor - Genegineers accomplished this. Sleepers don't have to like something for it to become real. Their oppositional reaction to it has power. When you fear the consequences of a thing whose possibility is in doubt, your fear fuels its acceptance into the Consensus.<br /> <br /> Progenitors: &quot;More food, anyone?&quot;<br /> Celestial Chorus: &quot;God does not allow this. You won't succeed.&quot;<br /> Sleepers: &quot;Feed staving children? Will God be angry?&quot;<br /> Progenitors: &quot;We are doing this anyway. We have the best lab in the world.&quot;<br /> Paradox Spirit: &quot;A little trial first. Check out this maze. Okay, careful next time.&quot;<br /> Chorus: &quot;Congregations, stop this!&quot;<br /> Sleepers: &quot;Rararararra!&quot; - discord, cable-news formula debates, talking points<br /> Factory Farmer: &quot;That's the tallest corn I've ever seen.&quot; <br /> Progenitors: &quot;You are welcome.&quot;<br /> Chorus: &quot;Let's raise money to ship the excess food to those who need it most.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-04T22:31:40-08:00","id":1421934,"title":"","content":"That's a paradigm shift, which is a way of changing the boundary between Vulgar and Coincidental. But again, Coincidental isn't the same as \u201ceveryone can do it\u201d. You've shifted the paradigm in terms of what the Consensus believes <i>you</i> can do. What I'm thinking of is this: once you've made <i>that</i> shift, how do you about the paradigm in terms of what the Consensus believes <i>they</i> can do? <br /> <br /> Or put another way: with your corn stalks, you've \u201cgiven the people fish, and you've fed them for a day\u201d. What you <i>want</i> to do is to \u201cteach them how to fish, so they'll be fed for life\u201d. How? <br /> <br /> It's Coincidental Magick now; but it's still Magick, which means that you need to be Awakened to perform it. How do you get things so that those who are still Sleepers can perform it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-04T23:02:16-08:00","id":1421935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1420194-population-growth-in-mystic-paradigm-parallel-world?p=1421934#post1421934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or put another way: with your corn stalks, you've \u201cgiven the people fish, and you've fed them for a day\u201d. What you <i>want</i> to do is to \u201cteach them how to fish, so they'll be fed for life\u201d. How?<br /> <br /> It's Coincidental Magick now; but it's still Magick, which means that you need to be Awakened to perform it. How do you get things so that those who are still Sleepers can perform it?</div> </div> </div> </div>When the farmer says, &quot;...tallest corn I've ever seen.&quot;<br /> and Progenitors say, &quot;You are welcome.&quot;, it's implied that they gave him the GMO seed. He can now replant from the seeds derived from the mature crop. The DNA of the crop has been permanently changed to produce increased yields. The farmer can now do &quot;Sleeper Sorcery&quot; by tilling, fertilizing, planting and watering. Further, Sleepers can alter DNA themselves, in labs, if they are geneticists. GMO is now part of the Paradigm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-04T23:13:30-08:00","id":1421936,"title":"","content":"I mean, literally everything the modern world in WoD is sleeper sorcery carried out by trained personnel. A doctor is someone with years of training in esoteric matters, has a mode of dress and conduct, gives you medicine made from things that you don't have and in ways you can barely imagine that has to be ingested in a particular way to give you an effect. A laboratory or a surgical suite is nothing more than a strange magical alter or the equivalent of a ritual circle to do shit. <br /> <br /> If Dataweaver's point was true, there would be no unAwakened programmers, Engineers, doctors, pilots, and detectives in the modern world, because near everything that is modern in Mage the Ascension was once something vulgar and conceived in the mind of an Enlightened Technocrat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-04T23:16:10-08:00","id":1421937,"title":"","content":"The shift to Sleeper Sorcery isn't enough; but it's a step in the right direction. <br /> <br /> But I don't know of any mechanism by which Awakened Magick can be turned into Sleeper Sorcery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-04T23:18:19-08:00","id":1421938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1420194-population-growth-in-mystic-paradigm-parallel-world?p=1421936#post1421936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, literally everything the modern world in WoD is sleeper sorcery carried out by trained personnel. A doctor is someone with years of training in esoteric matters, has a mode of dress and conduct, gives you medicine made from things that you don't have and in ways you can barely imagine that has to be ingested in a particular way to give you an effect. A laboratory or a surgical suite is nothing more than a strange magical alter or the equivalent of a ritual circle to do shit. <br /> <br /> If Dataweaver's point was true, there would be no unAwakened programmers, Engineers, doctors, pilots, and detectives in the modern world, because near everything that is modern in Mage the Ascension was once something vulgar and conceived in the mind of an Enlightened Technocrat.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you're missing my point. I'm not saying that it can't be done; I'm saying that it obviously can, but I don't know what the mechanism for doing it is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-04T23:30:21-08:00","id":1421939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1420194-population-growth-in-mystic-paradigm-parallel-world?p=1421938#post1421938\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think you're missing my point. I'm not saying that it can't be done; I'm saying that it obviously can, but I don't know what the mechanism for doing it is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, I say that it's the equivalent of large-scale engineering.<br /> <br /> Basically, do it the equivalent of a large scale project where you throw out propaganda, teach people, spread the word, convince people that it works. The equivalent of introducing ideas on genetic engineering or the first steam engine. Crazier stuff like hyperdrives or Iteration X HITMarks is a lot harder, but stuff like a better computer, things which naturally arise from previously known things (like the first lab-grown organs). Eat the paradox to get the first few working prototypes out in the public eye, and then as the Consensus reshapes, roll out more examples, until it turns normal. <br /> <br /> And of course your enemies are going to try and interfere. Burn down your genegineered crops. Induce malfunctions and failures into the prototype artificial kidneys. Spread lies and misinformation to weaken the consensus. All to stop this advancement. Which means you gotta crush them. <br /> <br /> If I knew more about WoD and the rules for large scale engineering inside them, I would try my hand at writing this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-04T23:34:49-08:00","id":1421940,"title":"","content":"Again, that's changing Vulgar to Coincidental. I don't have a problem with that. I'm looking at the <i>next</i> step, where you somehow turn Coincidental into Commonplace.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-04T23:44:59-08:00","id":1421941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1420194-population-growth-in-mystic-paradigm-parallel-world?p=1421940#post1421940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, that's changing Vulgar to Coincidental. I don't have a problem with that. I'm looking at the <i>next</i> step, where you somehow turn Coincidental into Commonplace.</div> </div> </div> </div>If any Sleeper can do it, it is commonplace.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-04T23:59:19-08:00","id":1421942,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1420194-population-growth-in-mystic-paradigm-parallel-world?p=1421940#post1421940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, that's changing Vulgar to Coincidental. I don't have a problem with that. I'm looking at the <i>next</i> step, where you somehow turn Coincidental into Commonplace.</div> </div> </div> </div>Um... ok? <br /> <br /> I mean, just repeat the process. Vulgar to Coincidental. Then Coincidental to Common place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-04T23:59:19-08:00","id":1421943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1420194-population-growth-in-mystic-paradigm-parallel-world?p=1421940#post1421940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, that's changing Vulgar to Coincidental. I don't have a problem with that. I'm looking at the <i>next</i> step, where you somehow turn Coincidental into Commonplace.</div> </div> </div> </div>Um... ok? <br /> <br /> I mean, just repeat the process. Vulgar to Coincidental. Then Coincidental to Common place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-05T10:25:31-08:00","id":1422063,"title":"","content":"Let me rephrase: how do you shift from \u201cMages only\u201d to \u201cSleeper access\u201d? Making Sleepers believe that something is possible is one thing; making them believe that <i>they</i> can do it is something else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-05T10:44:30-08:00","id":1422068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1420194-population-growth-in-mystic-paradigm-parallel-world?p=1422063#post1422063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let me rephrase: how do you shift from \u201cMages only\u201d to \u201cSleeper access\u201d? Making Sleepers believe that something is possible is one thing; making them believe that <i>they</i> can do it is something else.</div> </div> </div> </div>A Sleeper cannot distinguish between a Mage and other Sleepers. They do not know that the person who did the feat is anyone special. If a Mage makes it look easy, the Sleepers should be eager to try it out themselves, confidently.<br /> <br /> I realize this isn't going to satisfy your attention to detail. An example is needed. I will think on something and post when I have a bit more time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-05T10:46:04-08:00","id":1422070,"title":"","content":"...because that's literally the paradigm of the Technocracy? <br /> <br /> &quot;You too, can do this, if you had the right knowledge and training. The specialness isn't being chosen by the gods or chi. It's just knowledge.&quot; <br /> <br /> Sleepers don't see a difference between themselves and elder Technocrats. They only see a difference in education and training","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-05T11:41:56-08:00","id":1422082,"title":"","content":"\u2026and in that regard, part of the solution might be the Human Resources and Management Instrument: once you've got an Effect into the Coincidental column, it should be possible to work that Effect <i>through the actions of Sleepers</i>, where the mage directs their efforts but they do the work. Mechanically, it's still the mage performing an act of (Coincidental) Willworking; but from the Sleepers' perspective, their activities caused the result. <i>That</i> can strengthen the belief that anyone can do it once you know what you're doing. And over enough time, that might push the Effect into the realm of Hedge Magic, which Sleepers <i>can</i> learn and use without Awakened assistance. <br /> <br /> Being <i>told</i> \u201cyou can do it, too\u201d is no substitute for <i>actually doing it yourself</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-05T11:45:19-08:00","id":1422083,"title":"","content":"Urm... yes? That's what some Technocrats do? They lead and manage human resources to build infrastructure?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-05T11:48:21-08:00","id":1422085,"title":"","content":"Why the question marks?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-05T11:50:27-08:00","id":1422086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1420194-population-growth-in-mystic-paradigm-parallel-world?p=1422085#post1422085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why the question marks?</div> </div> </div> </div>Are we agreeing or disagreeing with one another?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-05T11:51:15-08:00","id":1422087,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure we're agreeing.<br /> <br /> Bringing this back to the original point of the thread: that's something a group like the Order of Hermes would have to do if they wanted to \u201cput their Magick into the hands of the common man\u201d: not <i>just</i> make it Coincidental, but also demonstrate that the common man can do it on their own. Human Resources is one way to do this; Wonders are another, as <i>that</i> convinces people that the Magick is in the Wonder, and that anyone who has the Wonder can do it. <br /> <br /> But in that regard, it only works if the Wonders are commonplace, which is hard to do without the Technocracy's edges in making Devices.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 11-05-2020, 03:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-05T22:15:01-08:00","id":1422179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1420194-population-growth-in-mystic-paradigm-parallel-world?p=1422087#post1422087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm pretty sure we're agreeing.<br /> <br /> Bringing this back to the original point of the thread: that's something a group like the Order of Hermes would have to do if they wanted to \u201cput their Magick into the hands of the common man\u201d: not <i>just</i> make it Coincidental, but also demonstrate that the common man can do it on their own. Human Resources is one way to do this; Wonders are another, as <i>that</i> convinces people that the Magick is in the Wonder, and that anyone who has the Wonder can do it.<br /> <br /> But in that regard, it only works if the Wonders are commonplace, which is hard to do without the Technocracy's edges in making Devices.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the modern WoD setting, the technocracy is engaged in Terra-Norming, a process of making individual Reality Zones internally uniform. This, they do in the hopes of later merging all the Earth's RZs into a single uniform Consensus without regional deviation. Even in a world with cell phones and the Internet, the dominant Mage faction is still having a hard time bringing it all together. <br /> <br /> In a Mythic Age type world, the geography would be divided up into many widely different Reality Zones. News travels slowly. A village can be a Reality Zone. Here, a Mage trying to make something coincidental and then commonplace isn't faced with the metaphysical atmospheric pressure of the whole world against his effect. <br /> <br /> Let's use an example. Classic fantasy. There are some craftsmen - and women - in the town who have skills that are vital and in demand. They make swords and only swordsmiths understand how to create a sword. Karthal the Hermetic alchemist wants to help the swordsmiths produce more swords so warriors can defend the village against goblins. <br /> <br /> Karthal has Mind 3, Prime 3, Matter 3. He inscribes runes on his metalworking tools to Enchant them. The Enchantment improves the tool's effectiveness, making it harder, sharper and also causing anyone who holds it to feel the power of the inscribed runes (Mind 3). He takes the tools to one of the swordsmiths while they are alone and offers the chance to use his special tools. <br /> <br /> Darina the Swordsmith tries out his tools. She feels the power of the runes giving the tools the improved usefulness for creating swords. &quot;How do you inscribe these runes of power?&quot;, she asks Karthal. He replies, &quot;Just wait until the full moon and speak these Magick words as you engrave the runes. I will go with you to the edge of the lake where the moonlight reflects its Magick. There, you can create enchanted tools of your own.&quot;. Darina agrees and meets Karthal at the time and place described.<br /> <br /> Now, Darina is using her own engraving instruments. As she goes through the ritual, Karthal casts the Magick silently, Enchanting her tools. He is using her actions as an Acolyte to focus his Magick. She now has tools that are enchanted for utility and have the same mind Effect that makes the user feel power coming from the runes. One by one, Karthal and Darina involve all of the swordsmiths in town in the moonlight ritual.<br /> <br /> Now, Karthal wants to build on the Mind enchantment while the smiths are not under its direct influence - so, not holding the engraved tools. He goes to the tavern where everyone goes to drink and socialize. He asks about how sword production is going. The smiths, who have put their tools away at home, thank Karthal for showing them the engraving ritual. Others in the vicinity overhear and inquire about these runes. The swordsmiths explain the new technique for enchanting. A bystander says, &quot;Is that how we ended up with so many superior swords? Ha! Now we can deal with those goblins. If it weren't for your runes, we would be facing being eaten by the goblins. So glad this new method exists.&quot;<br /> <br /> A young man seeking a trade hears of the power of the rune-using smiths and asks to be Darina's apprentice. He already believes in the effectiveness of the runes, because everyone in the village is sharing the good news. Darina shows him the ritual. The enchantment takes effect as he performs the ritual. It is no longer a Magickal effect, but physical law of the local Reality Zone that can be used as needed. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-06T04:02:35-08:00","id":1422215,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar26467_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26467\" data-vbnamecard=\"26467\">HorizonParty2021</a> That's the spirit.<br /> <br /> However, I think the process will take a little more effort and time. If everyone was able to teach magick with some little trickery on the local comunity, all mage acolites would be able to do it. However WoD shows us that actually being able to do Linear Magic takes some serious effort and willpower on part of the sleeper. And the mechanization of magick that the Technocracy made possible it's a step further in that direction.<br /> <br /> Darina the Swordsmith believing she can imbue the swords with magick because you did a trick and convincing the local people that she can do it are both steps on the rigth direction, but I think Darina's apprentice can't be just a random person. The apprentice will need to be actually compromised and have some serious willpower to be able to learn the enchantment, becoming a linear mage. As more people do that, the thing will become easier to teach, and eventually commonplace (or almost commonplace, in the way sleepers can learn medicine and use it, but they still need to study)<br /> <br /> That's the way Technocracy does it: First they have mages show that the experiment migth work to sleeper agents (altrough only in controled lab environments). They teach these &quot;experts&quot; to do it on their own (teaching linear magic). At the same time they advertise the method, and latter start to send their experts - first into places where people it's already very much convinced of the Technocratical Paradigm (academia, hig-tech corporations, and such - institutions that most likely are under supervision of the Technocracy), then into the public domain. After that, it becomes commonplace.<br /> <br /> I don't think the Hermetic approach would be so much trough Wonders as trough teaching (albeit I don't think that would be impossible, especially if House Verditus becomes more powerful).<br /> <br /> This process will likely take more time for Hermetics than it did for the Technocracy, because the latter rushed towards this revolutions as one of their foundational goals (to give power to the common man was deeply ingrained in Craftmason philosophy), but I think - I'm almost certain - that it would happen eventually. Because that's how humanity rolls, we like to live better lives within our understanding of what's better.<br /> <br /> Hermetics already teach people to use linear magic. If they had more people, I could see this education system branching into lesser lodges of linear mages that would be left in charge of improving the life of the comunities in little ways (building better houses, making lesser wards, helping with the goblins...you know).<br /> <br /> Since hermetics tend to be very absorbed in their own enligthenment, and treat linear magic as lesser, probably the next step to make things commonplace would have to be an initiative coming from these lesser lodges - these would need more people becuse the small and mundane problems are quite a lot, and Hermetics migth consent even uninitiated to be shown some lesser tricks. This could end cementing some sort of &quot;technology&quot; - runes, enchantments, and such - as something almost anyone can do and benefit from (like anyone can do maths).<br /> Because people likes stuff, who knows, maybe mystical Wonders start becoming common tech too - but then, maybe not: maybe society evolves to become less materialistic and more intelectual or mystical under Hermtic Paradigm","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 11-06-2020, 07:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-06T08:14:01-08:00","id":1422250,"title":"","content":"That's more or less what I was thinking. In particular, creating Linear Magic Paths in this way should be doable, but slow \u2014 and I'm not sure that getting the folks in a single Reality Zone to buy into the Path would be enough. This is mainly because Paths don't appear to be a thing that's Reality Zone dependent \u2014 though that may just be a legacy of the notion of Paths being conceived before the notion of Reality Zones was? Like I said, I'm not sure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-07T17:05:24-08:00","id":1422517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1420194-population-growth-in-mystic-paradigm-parallel-world?p=1422215#post1422215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[USER=&quot;26467&quot;]WoD shows us that actually being able to do Linear Magic takes some serious effort and willpower on part of the sleeper.</div> </div> </div> </div>This makes for good story concepts. It also does something that I like. It emphasizes the importance of using other means than the Mind Sphere to influence Sleepers. Spending Willpower is, by definition, a voluntary act. The Sleeper must want this Magick to work badly enough to spend Willpower. If the incentive isn't powerful enough to encourage the Sleeper to spend the WP, the attempt to introduce the Path Effect is hampered by the Sleeper whose attempt fails.<br /> <br /> If we're talking about Hermetics cloistered in Chantries, there is a lot of room for old, inhuman NPCs to devise scenarios where Sleepers who don't try hard enough are eliminated. Place the runes on the sword and tell the warrior wielding it to invoke it's power through an activation word and force of will. Those who believe get flaming swords. Those who don't spend the WP are the goblins' preferred target. In this case, the goblins are an existing threat. A truly devious NPC could manufacture the danger to weed out non-believers.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-08T13:05:44-08:00","id":1422647,"title":"","content":"As others have mentioned its about general welfare/standard of living improvements (not just food, but health and safety) generally to the point that you minimize mortality rates and maximize birthrates. That sort of approach (again as others note) seems best suited to the Order of Reason/Technocratic Union because you're talking 'mass production' of magical solutions and that's more or less what they've been trying to do. I don't think it means you have to make everyone an 'active' user of magic so much as a consumer - the key things is that they benefit from the effects on a large enough scale that human gains outstrip losses by some margin.) Consensus can help here, as can making use of Enlightened Citizens (that's the term for technocratic 'sorcerer-equivalents') to help production rates. Not everyone needs to know how to make a car, or a gun, or manufacture aspirin. But as long as they have some instruction in its use, they can enjoy its benefits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25533-mister_dunpeal","name":"Mister_Dunpeal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-08T13:36:15-08:00","id":1422653,"title":"","content":"I like the notion of a Hermetic version relying more on training than on tools; but I'd say that they'd somehow push the training enough into the Consensus that you wouldn't need to be initiated into arcane secrets (in game terms, taking dots in Sorcery Paths), but instead would be able to pull off the sorts of stuff that we could expect from Sorcery simply with average, everyday use of the standard Abilities: training in Medicine would include knowing what runes to draw and which mystical correspondences to invoke, for example.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 11-09-2020, 09:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}